Files in this directory:

There are four fastq files used for teaching students to use dada2 and interpreting its output. The fastq files  were generated by sequencing a mock community (e.g. a sample of DNA created by adding known ququantities of DNA from a collection of different species). In some of these samples (Even), the same amount of DNA is added from every species. In other samples (staggered), different amounts of DNA are added from different species. "Processed" means that the fastq file has been quality controlled with the software "Trimmomatic" by the sequencing provider. "Raw" means that the fastq has not been quality-controlled. "Raw Even" and "Processed Even" are exactly the same sequencing data, except that the latter has been quality controlled by the sequencing provider. The same is true for "Raw Staggered" and "Processed Staggered". 

Key to data:
PE = processed even
PS = processed staggered
RE = raw even
RS = raw staggered

This directory also contains several other learning datasets. 
"Trio.RDS" contains the same four fastq files, processed with qiime, mothur, and dada2 and combined into a single phyloseq object.

"HMPv35.RDS" contains the complete Human Microbiome Project 16S rRNA data with limited metadata, and is used for many exercises. 

"HMP_simPH.RDS" is the subset of HMPv35 that contains only the vaginal samples. Each sample has been assigned a random pH. The pH values are not accurate - this is only a teaching exercise for data analysis with a continuous covariate. 
